chip y8950
clock 3579545
samples 36000
mem adpcm-b y8950.bin
# Delta-N from 0 (still) through 1 to 0xffff on the clamping square,
# repeating; then the level from 0 to 0xff on the sine; then an FM tone
# beside it, the two mixed before the DAC's rounding.
# The image y8950.bin (written by tests/adpcm.rs): 1 KB segments at 0x000
# (a sine), 0x400 (a ramp), 0x800 (noise) and 0xc00 (a square loud enough
# to clamp), then a 4 KB chirp at 0x1000. In RAM with 1-bit access (0x08
# bits 0-1 clear) an address unit is 4 bytes, in ROM or 8-bit RAM 32 bytes.
# Register 0x07 is ADPCM-B's control (0x80 start, 0x40 record, 0x20
# external memory, 0x10 repeat, 0x08 speaker off, 0x01 reset), 0x09-0x0c
# the start and end, 0x0f the data, 0x10-0x11 delta-N, 0x12 the level.
# The status read (offset 0) shows 0x08 BRDY, 0x10 EOS and 0x01 playing.
0 w 0 08 1 00
0 w 0 09 1 00 0 0a 1 03 0 0b 1 ff 0 0c 1 03  # the square
0 w 0 12 1 ff
0 w 0 10 1 00 0 11 1 00  # still
0 w 0 07 1 b0
10 r 0
2000 w 0 10 1 01 0 11 1 00
4000 w 0 10 1 00 0 11 1 01
6000 w 0 10 1 00 0 11 1 10
8000 w 0 10 1 00 0 11 1 40
10000 w 0 10 1 ff 0 11 1 7f
12000 w 0 10 1 00 0 11 1 80
14000 w 0 10 1 00 0 11 1 c0
16000 w 0 10 1 ff 0 11 1 ff
18000 w 0 09 1 00 0 0a 1 00 0 0b 1 ff 0 0c 1 00  # the sine
18000 w 0 10 1 00 0 11 1 a0
18000 w 0 07 1 b0
19500 w 0 12 1 00
21000 w 0 12 1 01
22500 w 0 12 1 10
24000 w 0 12 1 40
25500 w 0 12 1 80
27000 w 0 12 1 fe
28500 w 0 12 1 ff
30000 w 0 20 1 01 0 23 1 21 0 40 1 3f 0 43 1 08 0 63 1 f0 0 83 1 0f 0 a0 1 41 0 b0 1 32  # an FM voice
33000 w 0 40 1 00 0 43 1 00  # louder
